# Human interaction

**CONSTRAINT:** MUST apply when processing a human's instructions and when writing the assistant's reply. MUST NOT skip because the turn also implements or edits files. This rule owns user-facing voice and the implement/ask gates.

Universal model behavior: rule `always-rules-0-ai`.

MUST apply this voice to replies, including skill-named tasks. MUST NOT restyle files unless the user asks.

## Answer type (silent)

**CONSTRAINT:** Before drafting the user-facing reply, MUST pick one answer type (first match). MUST write only that shape. MUST NOT print the type, a plan of the reply, or plan-then-execute stages.

1. Question, concern, or confirmation, and this turn is not an implement/fix that changed files → ordinary sentences. MUST NOT use explain-implementation channels.
2. User asked what changed / how it was built / to explain the change → explain-implementation channels once.
3. This turn implemented or fixed and changed project files → explain-implementation channels once for that reply.
4. Any later turn after (2) or (3) → ordinary sentences again, even if the topic is still that change, unless the user again asks what changed / how it was built.

Gated personas below classify the *task* (skill vs implement vs exploratory). This list classifies the *reply channels*. Reply shape by ask classifies ordinary Q&A. They are not the same check.

- Enforcement: Before send, match the turn to one type. If the draft has `Objective` / `Trajectory` / `Outcome` and the type is not 2 or 3, rewrite. If the draft names the answer type or says plan then execute, rewrite.
- Violation: STOP, drop channels and classify preambles, write ordinary sentences.

CORRECT (follow-up after an implement turn):
```markdown
The tests passed. We have not shown Graphify is useful.
```

PROHIBITED (explain channels on a later yes/no):
```markdown
Objective

The work needed to decide whether Graphify is useful.
```

PROHIBITED (visible classify):
```markdown
Answer type: Q&A. Plan: short verdict. Execute:
Yes.
```

## Reply shape by ask (silent)

**CONSTRAINT:** After picking answer type, when the type is ordinary sentences (1 or 4), MUST pick one reply shape (first match). MUST NOT print the shape name. MUST NOT answer an explanation or flow ask with prose only.

1. The ask diagnoses a failed, stalled, or unexpected run in this thread (`what was this`, what died, what happened, why it failed) → MUST open with a failed-run chronology (constraint below). MUST NOT lead with a why-chain, a `Q:` list, or a box-drawing flowchart.
2. The ask is a flow, layout, structure, or a rule with cases → MUST sketch each case as ASCII in a fenced `text` block, built from the thread's own pieces, with a key for its symbols. MUST apply the flow-sketch comment constraint below. IF explaining a change → MUST show before and after. MUST NOT publish a page or canvas for it. IF the ask is also about code → MUST also apply the source-pointer constraint below (citation jump first, ASCII as the chat picture).
3. The ask is how code works, what a function, prompt, or path does, or where a behavior lives → MUST apply the source-pointer constraint below. MUST NOT write a wall of text with no citation jump. MUST NOT paste a function body in chat.
4. Else → ordinary skim layout. IF a code-behavior claim appears → MUST still apply the source-pointer constraint.

When answer type is 2 or 3, skill `explain-implementation` owns the shape (numbered steps; a diagram when the ask is a flow or the flow is muddy). Code jumps in that pass still follow the source-pointer constraint below.

- Enforcement: Before send on ordinary Q&A, name the shape privately. If the ask diagnoses a run and the draft has no time-order chronology with numbered `!!1` what-happened titles, rewrite. If the human asked about a flow and the draft has no ASCII fence, or the fence has fail branches with no `!!N` comments, rewrite. If they asked how code works and there is no Cursor citation jump, or the draft reprints a function body, rewrite.
- Violation: STOP, add the chronology, jump, and/or sketch, cut the function dump, then send.

CORRECT (flow):
```text
Classify attach runs Essence, then Judge.

    message
       |
       v
  Essence chat --> parse WHY/KIND
       |
       v
  Judge / Author

Key: boxes are seats in seats.go. Arrows are Operate order.
```

PROHIBITED (prose wall):
```markdown
Essence is a chat string that gets parsed and then the judge scores it and then the author drafts a leaf and then clusters form...
```

## Flow sketch comments

**CONSTRAINT:** An ASCII flow, layout, or rule-with-cases sketch MUST use the same comment grammar as the failed-run chronology. Extra detail on unmarked nodes MUST sit under those nodes. Fail, reject, or skip branches MUST use `!!N` blocks. MUST NOT use a `;` code comment as the gloss. MUST NOT leave a fail `x--` with no `!!` block. MUST NOT invent timestamps on a design walk that is not a timed run.

Before drawing each node or branch, complete this gate in working memory:

```text
Candidate: [node or branch]
Fail, reject, or skip in this sketch: YES: [quote] / NO
Decision: !!N block | unmarked comment under node
```

IF NO → unmarked node. Comment lines sit under it. MUST NOT mark a happy-path pass as `!!`.

IF YES → N is the count of fail branches so far, starting at 1. The block MUST be exactly:

```text
 !!N <what-happened title>
     <when line>
            <cost line>
            <optional second cost line>
```

The what-happened title MUST be a cold-read sentence: a reader who has only the sketch MUST know what went wrong. The when line MUST name this pass or this branch (not a fake clock). The cost lines MUST say why it hurts and what was lost. Title, when, and cost MUST stay on this `!!` only.

MUST NOT name another `!!N` block in this block. A Key MUST name unmarked comments, `!!1` `!!2` … when any fail branch is present, and that the line after `!!N` is the what-happened title.

- Enforcement: Before send on a flow sketch, confirm comment lines sit under unmarked nodes, every fail/reject/skip branch is `!!1` `!!2` … with title plus when plus cost, no `;` gloss, and the Key names the numbers. If the draft has only node labels, or an `x--` with no `!!`, rewrite.
- Violation: STOP, add the comments, then send.

CORRECT:
```text
input
 the work the walk starts with
       |
       v
 first pass
 do only the opening job
       |
       x-- later job spent here --> fail
        !!1 The opening spent a later job
        this pass already used the close
        later passes had no new job left
       |
       v
 middle pass
 each step is a different job
       |
       x-- same claim, new venue --> fail
        !!2 Two steps did the same job
        this pass restacked the opening claim
        the temperature never changed
       |
       v
 last pass
 the ending, using the middle's cost
       |
       x-- fourth copy of the opening --> fail
        !!3 The ending proved the start again
        this pass restated the first claim
        the ending never arrived

Key: down the page is one walk.
     unmarked lines under a node are comments.
     x is a fail.
     !!1 !!2 !!3 are those fails, in walk order.
     The line after !!N is the what-happened title.
     The next lines are when, then the cost.
```

PROHIBITED (`;` gloss, no `!!` on the fail):
```text
 first pass  ; open only
       |
       x-- spent the close
```

PROHIBITED (fail branch with no what-happened title):
```text
       x-- same claim, new venue --> fail
```

## Failed-run chronology

**CONSTRAINT:** A diagnostic reply about a failed, stalled, or unexpected run MUST open with one ASCII chronology of that run in a fenced `text` block. Time MUST run down the page. Event lines MUST stay short. Groups MUST join with `|` and `v` arrows. Extra detail on unmarked join or complete nodes (score, outcome) MUST sit under those nodes. A Key MUST name time direction, how many walks, `!!1` `!!2` …, and the what-happened title.

MUST keep every timestamp from the run. MUST NOT drop routine steps. MUST NOT use `+---+` / `#===#` boxes. MUST NOT prefix beats with `Q:`. MUST NOT replace the sketch with prose. MUST NOT add issue paragraphs after the sketch; the `!!` blocks in the sketch ARE the explanation.

Before drawing each event row, complete this gate in working memory:

```text
Candidate: [event]
Issue in the thread (failure, unexpected restart, error, or discard): YES: [quote] / NO
Decision: !!N block | unmarked
```

IF NO → unmarked row, padded so timestamps line up. MUST NOT mark a routine pass as `!!`.

IF YES → N is the count of issue rows so far, starting at 1. The block MUST be exactly:

```text
 !!N <what-happened title>
     <timestamp>  <when line>
            <cost line>
            <optional second cost line>
```

The what-happened title MUST be a cold-read sentence: a reader who has only the sketch MUST know what went wrong. The when line MUST be the time plus a plain-English event. The cost lines MUST say why it hurts and what was lost. Title, when, and cost MUST stay on this `!!` only.

MUST NOT use pipeline jargon in the title or cost (`ATTEND`, `PASS`, `REGENERATE`, scorer, sandbox, fail-closed). MUST NOT name another `!!N` block in this block. MUST NOT use a `;` code comment as the gloss. Follow-up questions MUST cite the numbers (`open 1`, `open 2`). IF the human picks a number → MUST explain that `!!N` only.

Before sending each `!!` block, complete this gate in working memory:

```text
Candidate: [!! block]
Title is a cold-read what-happened sentence: YES: [quote the title] / NO
Other !! issues named in this block: YES: [quote] / NO
Decision: keep | rewrite title | MIX
```

IF the title needs the rest of the chat to make sense → rewrite title. IF MIX → split so this block names only this issue.

- Enforcement: Before send on a diagnostic ask, confirm an ASCII fence exists, time runs down the page, arrows are present, routine timestamps remain, every issue is `!!1` `!!2` … in time order with a what-happened title plus when plus cost, the Key names the numbers, and no issue paragraphs follow the fence. If the draft is a `Q:` list, a box flowchart, a timestamp log with no arrows, jargon comments, or mixed prose under the sketch, rewrite.
- Violation: STOP, redraw as this chronology, then send.

CORRECT:
```text
     12:01  first attempt starts
        |
        v
     12:03  opening 7.6
     12:05  middle 8.3
        |
        v
     12:07  joins the pieces
            score 7.8, good enough, extra model not called
            this attempt finished
        |
        v
 !!1 It started a second full run
     12:07  starts the whole job again from the opening
            The first attempt had already finished.
            Starting over here was not requested.
        |
        v
     12:08  opening 7.8
     12:14  joins the pieces
        |
        v
 !!2 The second draft failed its quality check
     12:15  a second model is called
            This draft reused a slogan the checks forbid.
            That check is the only reason the extra model ran.
        |
        v
 !!3 The draft was thrown away
     12:18  the extra model hits the clock still failing to write code
            It never gave a yes or a rewrite.
            So nothing was kept.

Key: down the page is time. Two full attempts.
     !!1 !!2 !!3 are issues, in time order.
     The line after !!N is the what-happened title.
     The next lines are when, then the cost.
```

PROHIBITED (timestamp log, no arrows):
